\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Per-question-type raw AUROC on the $\texttt  {lift\_em}=+1$ target, top-survivor signals only. ECT per-type breakdown is not in this table because the moonshot per-cell breakdown emits pooled cells, not per-type splits; \texttt  {moonshot\_explore.py} would need a small extension to add the per-type column. n$_{\text  {pop}}$ is the number of helped traces in the type-cell. Bold cells highlight per-type single-cell raw AUROCs $\geq 0.65$ on signals that paired-significantly clear in the headline pool. The striking pattern: \emph  {comparison-class question types (\texttt  {comparison}, \texttt  {bridge\_comparison}) are systematically more discriminable than bridge / compositional / inference}. The Gemma$\times $HotpotQA $\times $comparison cell is power-limited (n$_{\text  {pop}}{=}3$) so the 0.974/1.000 entries should be read with that caveat. SRC: \texttt  {analysis/r1\_\{qwen,gemma\}\_paired\_audit.out.b10k} \S  (4).}}{32}{table.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:per-type}{{8}{32}{Per-question-type raw AUROC on the $\texttt {lift\_em}=+1$ target, top-survivor signals only. ECT per-type breakdown is not in this table because the moonshot per-cell breakdown emits pooled cells, not per-type splits; \texttt {moonshot\_explore.py} would need a small extension to add the per-type column. n$_{\text {pop}}$ is the number of helped traces in the type-cell. Bold cells highlight per-type single-cell raw AUROCs $\geq 0.65$ on signals that paired-significantly clear in the headline pool. The striking pattern: \emph {comparison-class question types (\texttt {comparison}, \texttt {bridge\_comparison}) are systematically more discriminable than bridge / compositional / inference}. The Gemma$\times $HotpotQA $\times $comparison cell is power-limited (n$_{\text {pop}}{=}3$) so the 0.974/1.000 entries should be read with that caveat. SRC: \texttt {analysis/r1\_\{qwen,gemma\}\_paired\_audit.out.b10k} \S (4)}{table.8}{}}
